[Better Approach 2] Using Bottom-Up DP (Tabulation)-O(m*n) time and O(m*n) space
Use a tableto store solutions of subproblems to avoiding recalculate the same subproblems multiple times.

Before building the solution, we need to initialise the table with the known values i.e. base case. Here m = 0 and n = 0 is the situation of the base case, so we initialise first-column dp[i][0] with i and first-row dp[0][j] with j.
- Building the solution of larger problems from the smaller subproblems: We can easily define the iterative structure by using the recursive structure of the above recursive solution.
- if (s1[i - 1] == s2[j - 1]) dp[i][j] = dp[i - 1][j - 1];
- if (s1[i - 1] != s2[j - 1]) dp[i][j] = 1 + min(dp[i][j - 1], dp[i - 1][j], dp[i - 1][j - 1]);
