The idea is to generate the i-th Gray code directly using the formula:

^ (i >> 1)
The generated Gray codes are:
- Gray(0) = 0 ^ 0 = 0 -> 000
- Gray(1) = 1 ^ 0 = 1 -> 001
- Gray(2) = 2 ^ 1 = 3 -> 011
- Gray(3) = 3 ^ 1 = 2 -> 010
- Gray(4) = 4 ^ 2 = 6 -> 110
- Gray(5) = 5 ^ 2 = 7 -> 111
- Gray(6) = 6 ^ 3 = 5 -> 101
- Gray(7) = 7 ^ 3 = 4 -> 100
Thus, the generated 3-bit Gray code sequence is: 000 001 011 010 110 111 101 100
